x_tokens": 128000, "output_config.effort": "high", "thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 1337, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 1337, "cached_input": 53840, "input": 55179, "output": 165}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 73677, "other": 423, "system": 36306, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 42293}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 167096}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "bdb45ed0-810a-57d6-849e-efbe5ae2b5d5", "at": 1795640904.7385025, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 41697, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "5e46b71d66194c2a2017f9e9c058e1ce", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "196f27b1-7e71-5dce-9908-ce4ef57a3713", "at": 1795640904.7448614, "until": 1795640906.2857895, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 41698, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "5e46b71d66194c2a2017f9e9c058e1ce", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_017KBWSqJtDdmsjWw3Ux5m62", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian && cp story-wiki/Outline.md /tmp/outline5.md; rm -rf story-wiki && git clone -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" story-wiki 2>&1 | tail -2; diff /tmp/outline5.md story-wiki/Outline.md | head -150", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian && cp story-wiki/Outline.md /tmp/outline5.md; rm -rf story-wiki && git clone -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" story-wiki 2>&1 | tail -2; diff /tmp/outline5.md story-wiki/Outline.md | head -150"]], "output": "```console\n75c75,76\n< - **The sampling noise is not the bottleneck; the value function is.** Two independent runs agree on the top-3 set at 0.94–1.00 at the default budget, while *exact* explanations under a different 50-row background agree at 0.57–0.69 (German, ACS-Employment) and under retrained models at 0.14–0.83. This reorients the story's message: the single run is a reliable estimate of *the attribution it targets*; that target is itself far less stable than the run. M6 therefore moves from a yardstick to a co-headline (Fig 2 + Fig 5 are the pair), with its limits: floors on subsets (German MLP n=10, K=6; ACS-Income MLP bootstrap kept 3 of 40 models), N = 2 non-trivial populations for the default-budget claim.\n---\n> - **The value function is less stable than the run, at B=50 (rev 6: scoped after idea-review, issue #6).** Two independent runs agree on the top-3 set at 0.94–1.00 at the default budget, while *exact* explanations under a different 50-row random background agree at 0.57–0.69 (German, ACS-Employment). That floor b is itself a finite-sample effect of B=50 (noise from drawing B rows, which should shrink with B) mixed with a choice of reference distribution (which does not). Until the B ∈ {20, 50, 200} and k-means-50 cells exist, the paper states this **only as \"at B=50\"** and does not write \"the background, not the run, is the bottleneck\" as a general claim; floor b is reported as a function of B on the same instances as floor a, and k-means vs random is a separate entry. Floor c (retrain) is reported as its three definitions (bootstrap, seed, hyperparameter) side by side, each with n and K, never as one range; it rests on one seed and one trained model per population in the main cells, the MLP bootstrap kept 3 of 40 models in ACS-Income, German MLP has n=10, K=6, and it is the weakest number of the three floors, so it does not go in the abstract as a number. The headline's CI is over instances of one trained model: training variance is not in it, and the scope sentence says so. M6 is a co-headline by my choice of emphasis *after* seeing results (post hoc emphasis, marked as such in the paper); the pre-registered readings (H1 rule, R1 contrast) are kept as written. Fig 2 + Fig 5 are the pair.\n>   - *rev 7, partial B-sensitivity (`background_reference_shift.csv`; German, ACS-Employment, up to 30 instances, German RF n=9–10):* the exact top-3 set of the B=50 reference stays the same under B=20 for 23–47%, under k-means-50 for 50–89%, under B=200 for 46–100% of instances. So the reference's top-3 depends on the background draw even at B=200 against B=50, and it moves toward stability with B but does not settle; this is *not yet* the floor-b-vs-B curve (that needs two independent draws at each B, same instances as floor a), so the paper still says \"at B=50\" and presents these as reference shifts, with n. **German MLP retraining floors are unusable** (AUC filter kept 1/24 bootstrap and 3/24 hyperparameter retrainings; only `c_seed` kept 6/15): the paper shows floor c for German MLP as not available, not as a number.\n77c78,79\n< - **M5 as reported:** slope of φ-error vs m ≈ −0.5 for the unbiased paired estimator (estimator check passes); shap `l1_reg=False` ≈ −0.7 (ill-conditioned below m ≈ 3d); `num_features(10)` ≈ 0 (biased, does not converge: share 0.68–0.87 at default). The m* ∝ 1/g² relation is **not confirmed as stated**: median log-log slope ≈ −1.07 vs −2 (censored instances excluded). The paper reports the fit and its CI as such; before it is written up as a refutation `analysis` should check that the grid (budgets spaced by ×2–×4; instances already reaching the target at the smallest budget) and the use of the margin g alone, instead of the per-instance noise scale σ_k of the Brief's H3 model, do not produce the flat slope (asked in issue #5 reply).\n---\n> - **M5 as reported (rev 7, `mstar_tobit.csv`, replaces the interpolated −1.07):** slope of φ-error vs m ≈ −0.5 for the unbiased paired estimator (estimator\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "1eaacde0-5e8c-522a-ba4c-369ff3e7da8f", "at": 1795640905.9392438, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 41713, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "5e46b71d66194c2a2017f9e9c058e1ce", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "9f20efd2-b131-561d-b592-dc760d3d3e1b", "at": 1795640905.9484332, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 41715, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "5e46b71d66194c2a2017f9e9c058e1ce", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "5d0c695f-79f2-55fb-aefb-4257994587a4", "at": 1795640905.9523273, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 41716, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "5e46b71d66194c2a2017f9e9c058e1ce", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "f0adc1b0-f995-529d-968d-1762915a9c24", "at": 1795640906.023436, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 41721, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "5e46b71d66194c2a2017f9e9c058e1ce", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repository": null, "